Portions of this software (the number-format grammar, the value-to-string
rendering algorithms, the built-in format table, and the associated edge-case
handling) are ported from ssf v0.11.2 and remain under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

Changes made in this port relative to the upstream JavaScript source:

  - Translated from JavaScript to Rust.
  - Calendar dates are derived from the date serial via pure civil-date
    arithmetic rather than the host `Date` object, making results deterministic
    and independent of the host timezone/DST.
  - The public formatting entry points return `Result` values instead of
    throwing on unsupported/invalid input.

Folio modifications (2026-09-19):
  - Exposed section selection for display colors and layout directives.
  - Rounded date/time fields together to carry seconds through midnight.
  - Returned an error for oversized fixed fraction denominators.

Folio modifications (0.35):
  - Added bounded format-shape validation and TEXT numeric formatting shared
    by the formula engine and cell renderer.
